truenas-mcp is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for TrueNAS.  It
runs on the local machine, connects to the TrueNAS API over a websocket
and lets an AI assistant query and manage the system.

It covers monitoring (system information, alerts, jobs, metrics),
storage (pools, datasets, snapshots, SMB and NFS shares), data
protection tasks, apps, system updates, boot environments, directory
services and virtual machine status.

The --read-only flag hides every tool that changes the system.
Destructive actions require explicit confirmation.  TrueNAS 25.10 or
later is required.
